hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"294","We are Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, we are Muadh, meaning Ibn Muadh Al-Anbari, we are Ikrimah bin Ammar Al-Yamimi, Abdullah bin Ubaid Allah bin Umair told us. Al-Laythi, said: Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to leach semen from his garment with the sweat of his idhikhar, and then he would pray in it.” And he washes some of his garment dry, then prays in it.” We have Muhammad bin Yahya, we have Abu Al-Walid, we have Ikrimah bin Ammar, similarly, except that he said: “With the sweat of Idhkhir from his garment and praying “In it,” she said: “And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to look at it dry, open it, and pray in it.”"
"295","We are Muhammad, meaning Ibn Yahya, we are Abu Qutaybah, we are Ikrimah, who is Ibn Ammar, we are Abdullah, who is Ibn Ubaid Ibn Umair, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a person in a state of impurity dry in his clothes, he would wipe them.”"
